This testcase verifies that a module whose load raised an exception is
not stored in the modules table.

A cached failed load made the next require() of the same name return
null without an error. Each require() must try the load again and
report the error again.

-- Testcase --
for (let i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
	try {
		print(require('broken'), "\n");
	}
	catch (e) {
		print(e.type, ": ", split(e.message, "\n")[0], "\n");
	}
}

print(exists(modules, 'broken'), "\n");
-- End --

